          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In general,
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            is a process of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} freely
            adjoining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverses"} inverses
            to an algebraic structure. In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %em localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}[W^{-1}]
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            at a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            is – if it exists (see below) – the result of universally making all morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            %strong localization functor
            is any functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C[W^{-1}]
            satisfying the universal property of the localization at some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %p
            Some authors call any localization of a category a
            %em category of fractions
            (
            %a{:href => "#GabrielZisman67"}> Gabriel &amp; Zisman, §1.1
            ;
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Borceux94"} Borceux 1994 I, Def. 5.2.1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"}> calculus of fractions
            ” (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Fritz11"} Fritz 2011
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Verdier96"} Verdier 1996, Def. 2.2.5
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#StacksProject"} Stacks Project
          %p
            Yet other authors take “localization” to mean specifically “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localizations"}> reflective localizations
            ”, by default (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Lurie 2009
          %h3#motivation Motivation
          %p
            A classic example is the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+commutative+ring"} localization of a commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            away from the prime
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\frac{1}{2}]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational numbers
          %p
            The terminology is odd for historical and geometric reasons: localizing
            %em at
            a prime means inverting things
            %em not
            divisible by that prime, while inverting the prime itself is called localizing
            %em away
            from that prime. The reason for this, as well as for the term ‘localization’, becomes more apparent when we consider examples of a more vividly geometric flavor.
          %p
            For example, the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}[x]
            consists of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            functions on the real line. If we pick a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbb{R}
            and localize
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}[x]
            by putting in an inverse to the element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x-a)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+function"} rational function
            %em everywhere
            on the real line
            %em except
            possibly at the point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                localization
                %em away from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            generated by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x-a)
          %p
            If on the other hand we put in an inverse to every element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}[x]
            that is
            %em not
            in the ideal
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %em somewhere
            on the real line
            %em at least
            at the point
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x-a)
            in the denominator. This is called
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                localizing
                %em at
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            Notice that what is literally ‘localized’ when localizing the ring is not the ring itself, but its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}[x]
            is the whole real line. When we localize away from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} - \{a\}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a\}
          %p
            The case of localizing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            can also be interpreted geometrically in a similar way, using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            theory and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
          %p
            A ring is a very special case of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            at a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is the universal solution to making the morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            into
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^{-1}C
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi W
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset Mor(C)
            a collection of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A
            %strong localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            (or “at
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a (generally
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            %li
              %p
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q : C \to C[W^{-1}]
                (localization functor);
            %li
              %p such that
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    for all
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi w
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi W
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in W
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(w)
                    is an
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                %li
                  %p
                    for any category
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    and any
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo :
                          %mi C
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to A
                    such that
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(w)
                    is an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                    for all
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi w
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi W
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in W
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi W
                          %mo :
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi W
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_W : C[W^{-1}] \to A
                    and a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural isomorphism
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi F
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi W
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi Q
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \simeq F_W \circ Q
                %li
                  %p
                    the map between
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor categories
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi Q
                          %mo :
                          %mi Funct
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi W
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi Funct
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\circ Q : Funct(C[W^{-1}], A) \to Funct(C,A)
                  %p
                    is
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
                    for every category
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p Note:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
                exists, it is unique up to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %li
              %p
                In 2-categorical language,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinverter"} coinverter
                of the canonical natural transformation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo →
                        %mi t
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\to t
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %mi W
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t:W\to C
                are the “source” and “target” functors and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                is considered as a full subcategory of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C ^{\mathbf{2}}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Contrary to what is sometimes asserted, the localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
              may generally be constructed when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is large, even only in ZF where “large” means definable by class formulas. See Remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ZF"}
              below. However, the localization might not be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is. The tools of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model categories
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category of a model category
          %h3#reflective_localization Reflective localization
          %p
            A special class of localizations are
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localizations"} reflective localizations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi W
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to L_W C
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi W
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W C \hookrightarrow C
          %p In such a case
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi W
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Q
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L_W C
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Q}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  C
          %p
            this adjoint exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi W
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W C
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            One shows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi W
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W C
            is – up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            – the full subcategory on the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
          %p
            More on this is at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+factorization+system"} reflective factorization system
          %h3#localizations_of_enriched_categories Localizations of enriched categories
          %p
            Given a symmetric closed monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with underlying ordinary category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0
            and a subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0
            containing the identities of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+enriched+category"} localization of an enriched category
          %h2#construction Construction
          %p
            There is a general construction of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            has special properties, most notably when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system"} factorization system
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
          %h3#general_construction General construction
          %p
            Given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \,\subset\, Mor(C)
            is a set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            (not necessarily forming a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^{op}
            denote the corresponding set in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                between two vertices
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
                are given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mi op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x,y)\coprod W^{op}(x,y)
          %p
            The arrows in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^{op}(x,y)
            are written as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f}
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in W(y,x)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒫
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}G
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            are given by the empty path beginning and ending at a given object. We introduce a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            on the morphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒫
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}G
            and quotient by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            generated by it to get
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
          %p
            The equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            is that generated by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for all objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ;
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x;id_x;x) \sim (x;\emptyset;x)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:x\to y
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:y\to z
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ;
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo ;
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x;f,g;z)\sim (x;g\circ f;z)
            %li
              %p
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:x\to y
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ;
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x;f,\overline{f};x)\sim (x;id_x;x)
              %p and
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ;
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo ;
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ;
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi y
                      %mo ;
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y;\overline{f},f;y)\sim (y;id_y;y)
          #ZF.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              With a little care, this general construction can be enacted even for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+categories"} large categories
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZF"} ZF
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P} G
              on a large graph
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P} G
              is a certain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partial function
              or functional relation from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(G)
              satisfying some conditions given by ZF formulas; each such relation is a “set” by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/replacement+axiom"} replacement axiom
              = succeed "-equivalence" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P} G
              might be large (hence themselves could not be elements of a class), we can always use
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott%27s+trick"} Scott's trick
              and consider instead those representatives in each equivalence class that have minimal ZF
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
              (using crucially the
              = succeed ");" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+foundation"} axiom of foundation
              = succeed "." do
                %em set
            %p
              The rub is that the localization might not be locally small, even if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is.
          %h3#construction_when_there_is_a_calculus_of_fractions Construction when there is a calculus of fractions
          %p
            If the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} spans
            instead of zig-zags. The idea is that any morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: x \to z
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            is built from a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mi y
                  %mo →
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_2 : y \to z
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mi y
                  %mo →
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1 : y \to x
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                  %mi y
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 2
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \stackrel{f_1}{\longleftarrow} y \stackrel{f_2}{\longrightarrow} z
          %p
            For more on this, see the entry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dorette+Pronk"} Dorette Pronk
            has extended this idea to construct a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+fractions"} bicategories of fractions
            where a class of 1-arrows is sent to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalences
          %h3#in_abelian_categories In abelian categories
          %p
            Localization is especially well developed in abelian setup where several competing formalisms and input data are used. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+abelian+category"} localization of an abelian category
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The localization of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
                of two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+weak+equivalences"} categories with weak equivalences
                is (if it exists) the product of their localizations
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msubsup
                        %mi W
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msubsup
                        %mi W
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (\mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{D})[ (W_{\mathcal{C}} \times W_{\mathcal{D}})^{-1} ]
                      \\;\;
                      \\simeq
                      \\;\;
                      ( \mathcal{C}[W_{\mathcal{C}}^{-1}] )
                      \\times
                      ( \mathcal{D}[W_{\mathcal{D}}^{-1}] )
                      \\,.
              %p
                This is because localization is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflector"} reflector
                into the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ideal"} exponential ideal
                of minimal categories with weak equivalences.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                examples of localizations of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+categories"} locally small categories
                that are
                %em not
                themselves locally small:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "#Krause08"} Krause 2008, Ex. 4.15
                %li
                  %p
                    %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/703354/58526"} math.SE.a/703354
          %h2#in_higher_category_theory In higher category theory
          %p
            The notion of localization of a category has analogs in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %p
            For
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-localization"} 2-localization
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            and the special case of reflective embeddings this is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"}> localization of an (∞,1)-category
              \.
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
            is presented by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                localization of a simplicial model category
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/localization+of+a+simplicial+model+category"} ?
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizing+subcategory"}> localizing subcategory
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizer"} localizer
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+at+an+object"} localization at an object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+localization"} essential localization
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quintessential+localization"} quintessential localization
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  reflective bicategory
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/reflective+bicategory"} ?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+localization"} monoidal localization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  localization of a simplicial model category
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/localization+of+a+simplicial+model+category"} ?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+ring"}> localization of a ring
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+commutative+ring"} localization of a commutative ring
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+module"} localization of a module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+model+categories"} localization of model categories
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %span.newWikiWord
                      localization of simplicial model categories
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/new/localization+of+simplicial+model+categories"} ?
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-localization"} p-localization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+type+at+a+family+of+functions"} localization of a type at a family of functions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colocalization"} colocalization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+fractions"} ring of fractions
          %h2#References References
          %p Authors who say “category of fractions” for the result of inverting any class of morphisms:
          %ul
            %li#GabrielZisman67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"}> Pierre Gabriel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Zisman"} Michel Zisman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calculus+of+fractions+and+homotopy+theory"} Calculus of fractions and homotopy theory
                %em Ergebnisse der Mathematik und ihrer Grenzgebiete
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 35
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-642-85844-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-85844-4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/GZ.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Borceux94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , §5.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                    vol. 1
              %blockquote
                %p (See also vols. 2 and 3 for examples of the theory in action in abelian categories, sheaf theory etc.)
          %p Authors who say “localization” for the result of inverting any class of morphisms:
          %ul
            %li#KashiwaraSchapira00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Kashiwara"}> M. Kashiwara
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/P.+Schapira"} P. Schapira
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 332
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/3-540-27950-4"} doi:10.1007/3-540-27950-4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/kashiwara2.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Localization_of_a_category"} Localization of a category
          %p
            and reserve “category of fractions” for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
          %ul
            %li#Fritz11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Fritz"}> Tobias Fritz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categories of Fractions Revisited
              %strong 15
              2 (2011) 19-38 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0803.2587"}> arXiv:0803.2587
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://morfismos.math.cinvestav.mx/sites/default/files/Upload/vol15-n2-3.pdf"} morfismos:vol15-n2-3
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Yekutieli19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Yekutieli"}> Amnon Yekutieli
              , Chapter 6 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Derived Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108292825"} doi:10.1017/9781108292825
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09640"} arXiv:1610.09640
          %p
            Authors who say “localization” for inverting with respect to a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
          %ul
            %li#Verdier96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Verdier"}> Jean-Louis Verdier
                , Def. 2.2.5 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Des Catégories Dérivées des Catégories Abéliennes
                %strong 239
                (1996) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/issues/AST_1996__239__R1_0"}> numdam:AST_1996__239__R1_0
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/AST_1996__239__R1_0.pdf"} pdf
            %li#StacksProject
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stacks+Project"}> Stacks Project
                ,
                %em 4.27 Localization in categories
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04VB"}> tag:04VB
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            With focus on localization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"}> Pierre Gabriel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Des+cat%C3%A9gories+ab%C3%A9liennes"} Des catégories abéliennes
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=BSMF_1962__90__323_0"} numdam:BSMF_1962__90__323_0
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Verdier96"} Verdier 1996
          %p
            Review of localization in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Localizations
              = succeed "," do
                %em Axiomatic, enriched and motivic homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 131
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-007-0948-5"} doi:10.1007/978-94-007-0948-5
          %p
            For
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
          %ul
            %li#Krause08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henning+Krause"}> Henning Krause
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Localization theory for triangulated categories
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.commalg.org/2006/08/13/workshop-on-triangulated-categories-leeds/"} Workshop on Triangulated Categories, Leeds 2006
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.1324"}> arXiv:0806.1324
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A
            %strong terminological discussion
            prompted by question in which sense “localization” is a descriptive term or not is archived ion
            = succeed "Forum" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://nforum.ncatlab.org/discussion/481/localization/?Focus=23461#Comment_23461"} here
          %p
            A formal implementation of Gabriel-Zisman localization in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+assistant"} proof assistant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Simpson05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              %em Explaining Gabriel-Zisman localization to the computer
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0506471"}> arXiv:math/0506471
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~carlos/themes/verif.html"} web
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT"} HoTT
            = succeed "-formalization" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-categories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"}> localization of an (∞,1)-category
            ) in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Shulman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/mikeshulman/HoTT/blob/master/Coq/Subcategories/LexReflectiveSubcategory.v"} HoTT/Coq/Subcategories/LexReflectiveSubcategory.v
          %p
            An original account of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+commutative+rings"} localization of commutative rings
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-localization"} p-local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            is
          %ul
            %li#Sullivan70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"}> Dennis Sullivan
              ,
              %em Localization, Periodicity and Galois Symmetry
              (The 1970 MIT notes) edited by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Ranicki"} Andrew Ranicki
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/surgery/gtop.pdf"} pdf
